# rule.forbid.hand-run-reviews

> **a driver never runs `rhx review` by hand. a review is summoned by the guard, or it does not happen.**

the invocation is the violation.

| situation | move |
|---|---|
| lane overflowed or bind wrong | edit `$route/<stone>.guard` (narrow `--paths-wout`/`--paths-with`, trim `--conversation`); the guard runs it. needs `rhx route.mutate grant get` (a human grants once) |
| lane out of budget | `rhx route.guard.budget --for review --add N` |
| rubric wants a different corpus | a new lane in the guard |
| you want a second opinion | enroll a peer ROLE (`rule.always.get-a-second-opinion-before-foreman`) |

test: **"am I about to invoke `rhx review`?"** yes → stop; the answer is a guard edit.

blocker: a `rhx review` by a driver, for any reason · a scoped re-run cited as a spent lever · a hand-run verdict cited as proof a lane is clean · an overflowed lane left unrepaired.
